# Vigilante detector eval corpus (JSONL).
#
# One labelled request per line. The built-in detector runs on the same
# enriched envelope a live flow produces, and `vigilante -mode eval` reports
# recall, precision, and false-positive rate by category.
#
#   vigilante -mode eval -eval-corpus deploy/eval/corpus.jsonl
#
# Fields: id, class (attack|benign), category, method, path, query, body,
# headers, note. Rotate the UA/query values instead of adding near-duplicates:
# the corpus is a regression gate, not a fuzzer.
